{"app":"spr-flow","version":3,"nodes":[{"id":"note","type":"info","position":{"x":-1430,"y":-614},"data":{"title":"Inverse design of a Tamm emitter by gradient descent (He et al. 2021, benchmark)","text":"M. He et al., Nat. Mater. 20, 1663 (2021), after their published code: air / (Ge / SiO)⁴ Ge / CdO / SiO; Ge n = 4.0, SiO n = 2.25 (as in the code), CdO: doped-semiconductor Drude (Nolen 2020) with the carrier density N as a Design variable.\n\nTarget (their set_target), a Target node (model): reflectance = baseline 1 − Lorentzian dip at 4237.3 nm (CO₂, FWHM 60 nm) − Gaussian dip at 3500 nm (σ = 20 nm), on their grid 1500–3499 cm⁻¹ (step 1 cm⁻¹). Two Curve match nodes compare with it: the full spectrum, and only the resonances (“only where the target is < 0.95”). Loss: MSE + 0.01·max squared error (metric “MSE + λ·max error²”).\n\nOptimization Engine: Adam with their schedule (the default settings of Adam): stage 1 = 200 steps at lr 0.01 on the resonance points only (Curve match “resonances”), stage 2 = 450 steps at lr 0.05 on the full spectrum, lr × 0.7 every 100 steps, 4 starts. Thicknesses 50–850 nm, N 0.4–4·10²⁰ cm⁻³ (sigmoid bounds, as in the code).\n\nDifferences from the code: the gradient is by finite differences (not automatic differentiation) and the whole spectrum is used at each step (no random mini-batches of wavelengths); the vacuum first layer of the code has no effect and is left out; their CdO effective mass uses (3πn)^⅔, reproduced here by C = 1.47·(3.14/π²)^⅔ in the standard (3π²n)^⅔ form.","color":"#8a93a6","width":440,"height":460}},{"id":"air","type":"material","position":{"x":-910,"y":-354},"data":{"materialId":"Air","color":"#f4f6fa","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"ge","type":"material","position":{"x":-910,"y":-142},"data":{"materialId":"user-ge-4","color":"#7b7f86","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"sio","type":"material","position":{"x":-910,"y":71},"data":{"materialId":"user-sio-225","color":"#9ec5e8","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"cdo","type":"material","position":{"x":-910,"y":283},"data":{"materialId":"user-cdo-nolen","color":"#c98b3a","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"vN","type":"variable","position":{"x":-1430,"y":283},"data":{"name":"N CdO (10²⁰ cm⁻³)","value":2.2,"min":0.4,"max":4,"integer":false}},{"id":"target","type":"target","position":{"x":650,"y":-1357},"data":{"name":"target","mode":"components","axis":"lambda","min":1500,"max":3499,"step":1,"components":[{"id":"base","type":"baseline","params":{"c":{"value":1,"fixed":false},"s":{"value":0,"fixed":false}}},{"id":"co2","type":"lorentz","params":{"A":{"value":-1.0000000000000215,"fixed":false},"x0":{"value":4237.28814,"fixed":false},"w":{"value":60,"fixed":false}}},{"id":"g","type":"gauss","params":{"A":{"value":-1.000038285811295,"fixed":false},"x0":{"value":3500,"fixed":false},"w":{"value":47.09640090061899,"fixed":false}}}],"bands":[{"lo":400,"hi":520,"value":0,"weight":1},{"lo":540,"hi":620,"value":1,"weight":1},{"lo":640,"hi":800,"value":0,"weight":1}],"field":"R","fitId":"","color":"#e15759","gridUnit":"cm-1"}},{"id":"stack","type":"combine","position":{"x":0,"y":236},"data":{"name":"Tamm emitter","count":10}},{"id":"wl","type":"param","position":{"x":0,"y":826},"data":{"quantity":"lambda","mode":"range","value":4237,"min":2850,"max":6670,"step":2}},{"id":"th","type":"param","position":{"x":0,"y":1062},"data":{"quantity":"theta","mode":"constant","value":0,"min":0,"max":80,"step":1}},{"id":"tmm","type":"compute","position":{"x":650,"y":236},"data":{"name":"Tamm emitter","polarization":"s"}},{"id":"mAll","type":"match","position":{"x":1274,"y":-448},"data":{"name":"full spectrum","field":"R","metric":"msemax","weight":1,"lo":{"$num":"NaN"},"hi":{"$num":"NaN"},"lambdaMax":0.01}},{"id":"mRes","type":"match","position":{"x":1274,"y":142},"data":{"name":"resonances","field":"R","metric":"msemax","weight":1,"lo":{"$num":"NaN"},"hi":{"$num"